    "rule": "pre-registered (cycle 24 N1), two gates, every verdict first-class. The statistic is the RE-ADDRESSING RATE R(N): the fraction of one common evaluation population that receives a different descriptor address under two independent derivations of size N \u2014 DR 0046's unit, because a niche is a whole address and edge distance is not the unit any ledger number is counted in. GATE 1 (mechanism): fit log R against log N; sampling theory for quantile estimates predicts a slope of -0.5. Judge it against the MEASURED spread of the per-track slopes at 2.0x, never against a constant \u2014 'sampling_limited' if theory lies inside the measured band (the protocol is sound and 600 is merely small), 'structurally_indeterminate' if the curve is materially flatter (no affordable population determines the edges), 'faster_than_sampling' if steeper. GATE 2 (practical): the derivation-induced movement in OCCUPIED-NICHE COUNT, against a MEASURED floor \u2014 the movement that same count shows when the edges are held fixed and the evaluation population is resampled. 'determined_at' is the smallest ladder size reaching that floor; 'not_determined_within_reach' is first-class. The two gates may disagree, and reporting only one of them would hide the finding.",
